{"title":"Career Roadmap — Research Associate","role":"Research Associate","summary":"A Research Associate in biotechnology conducts experiments, analyses biological data, develops or validates methods, maintains laboratory records and contributes to research projects in areas such as molecular biology, genetics, microbiology, bioprocessing, bioinformatics, pharmaceuticals, diagnostics, vaccines and agricultural biotechnology.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High — Biotechnology Engineering provides the multidisciplinary foundation required for laboratory research and industrial R&D. For long-term independent research leadership, postgraduate study is usually important."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Molecular biology, microbiology, biochemistry, laboratory techniques and research methodology"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Research Associate → Senior Research Associate / Research Scientist"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Scientist / Senior Scientist / Project Lead"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Principal Scientist, R&D Manager, Research Program Lead or academic research leader"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Core learning","Practical outcome"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Biology, chemistry, mathematics, physics, programming"},{"text":"Scientific and quantitative foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Biochemistry, microbiology, genetics, molecular biology"},{"text":"Core wet-lab capability"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Genetic engineering, cell culture, bioprocessing, bioinformatics"},{"text":"Conduct independent experiments"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Advanced biotechnology, research methodology, statistics and scientific writing"},{"text":"Complete a publication-oriented research project"}]]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Scientific Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong fundamentals in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"General chemistry"},{"text":"Organic chemistry"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Biology"},{"text":"Basic programming"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Scientific communication"},{"text":"Laboratory safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mini-project"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse a biological dataset or perform a basic laboratory study and document:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research question","Hypothesis","Method","Data","Statistical analysis","Conclusion"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Molecular & Microbiological Foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biochemistry"},{"text":"Microbiology"},{"text":"Genetics"},{"text":"Molecular biology"},{"text":"Immunology"},{"text":"Enzymology"},{"text":"Cell biology"},{"text":"Biostatistics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Develop laboratory skills in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Microscopy"},{"text":"Pipetting"},{"text":"Buffer preparation"},{"text":"DNA/RNA extraction"},{"text":"Gel electrophoresis"},{"text":"PCR"},{"text":"Bacterial culture"},{"text":"Basic protein analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project"},{"type":"p","text":"Perform a small experimental study such as:"},{"type":"flow","items":["DNA extraction","PCR","Gel electrophoresis","Data interpretation"]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Biotechnology Research Skills"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"h","text":"Molecular Biotechnology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"PCR/qPCR"},{"text":"DNA cloning"},{"text":"Recombinant DNA technology"},{"text":"Gene expression"},{"text":"Sequencing concepts"},{"text":"CRISPR fundamentals"},{"text":"Protein expression"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cell & Microbial Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mammalian cell culture"},{"text":"Microbial fermentation"},{"text":"Cell-based assays"},{"text":"Enzyme technology"},{"